WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.219
ALEX: On announcement day. Which
is different from in

00:00:02.219 --> 00:00:04.438
ALEX: production.

00:00:04.548 --> 00:00:07.148
RUFUS: A vendor claim about scale
and safety is

00:00:07.148 --> 00:00:09.748
RUFUS: not independent validation.
NVIDIA says this. The partners

00:00:09.748 --> 00:00:12.349
RUFUS: say they're integrating.
Whether it works as described

00:00:12.349 --> 00:00:14.949
RUFUS: in a live enterprise
environment is a separate

00:00:14.949 --> 00:00:17.549
RUFUS: question.

00:00:17.729 --> 00:00:20.920
JAMIE: And that's the real
continuity here — yesterday

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:24.110
JAMIE: we had an unresolved
argument about whether this

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:27.301
JAMIE: would be a genuine security
advance or expensive

00:00:27.301 --> 00:00:30.491
JAMIE: AI bureaucracy. Now we have
the actual product.

00:00:30.601 --> 00:00:33.163
ALEX: We do. And honestly, it
moves the needle.

00:00:33.163 --> 00:00:35.725
ALEX: Not because it solves the
problem — it

00:00:35.725 --> 00:00:38.286
ALEX: doesn't — but because doing
governance at the

00:00:38.286 --> 00:00:40.848
ALEX: hardware layer with identity
verification is more than

00:00:40.848 --> 00:00:43.410
ALEX: most enterprises have right
now.
